export declare const FUNCTION_TOOLS_PROMPT = "\nIf a function you call is unclear or wrong, read it with read_code and fix it with edit_code.\nSome functions are directory reducers. Call await someFolder.apply(reducer, ...args) to retain their edits and typed result. Call const proposal = await someFolder.propose(reducer, ...args) to try an edit without changing the receiving folder: proposal.folder is an immutable source snapshot, proposal.value its result. Evaluate proposal.folder, then await someFolder.accept(proposal) when justified; stale or foreign proposals fail. Use snapshot() to freeze source, snapshot.branch() for an independent population branch, and await someFolder.select(snapshot) to install the exact selected source from the same target. To improve a program repeatedly, await someFolder.iterateOn(step, initialState, ...fixedArgs).withMeasure(state => state.remaining).until(state => state.done). Here the receiver is a folder, so pass the step explicitly: someFolder.iterateOn(step, initialState, ...fixedArgs). This differs from a callable receiver: step.iterateOn(initialState, ...fixedArgs). The step receives a private folder and current JSON state, and returns the next state. The result is {folder, state}; each step commits source and state together and leaves the original folder unchanged. The nonnegative integer measure must decrease each step; semantic progress reviews remain active and cannot replenish it.\nAn explicit top-level return in eval stages the typed value and, when this reducer was applied to a folder, retains every change.";
